    <briefdescription>
<para>Argentinian calendars. </para>    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Holidays for the Buenos Aires stock exchange (data from <ulink url="http://www.merval.sba.com.ar/">http://www.merval.sba.com.ar/</ulink>): <itemizedlist>
<listitem>
<para>Saturdays </para></listitem>
<listitem>
<para>Sundays </para></listitem>
<listitem>
<para>New Year&apos;s Day, January 1st </para></listitem>
<listitem>
<para>Holy Thursday </para></listitem>
<listitem>
<para>Good Friday </para></listitem>
<listitem>
<para>Labour Day, May 1st </para></listitem>
<listitem>
<para>May Revolution, May 25th </para></listitem>
<listitem>
<para>Death of General Manuel Belgrano, third Monday of June </para></listitem>
<listitem>
<para>Independence Day, July 9th </para></listitem>
<listitem>
<para>Death of General José de San Martín, third Monday of August </para></listitem>
<listitem>
<para>Columbus Day, October 12th (moved to preceding Monday if on Tuesday or Wednesday and to following if on Thursday or Friday) </para></listitem>
<listitem>
<para>Immaculate Conception, December 8th </para></listitem>
<listitem>
<para>Christmas Eve, December 24th </para></listitem>
<listitem>
<para>New Year&apos;s Eve, December 31th </para></listitem>
</itemizedlist>
</para>    </detaileddescription>
